1
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,094
CREATIVE ONIGIRI SHOP
BEEMUS

2
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,345
Good morning.

3
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:15,598
One Minami Minamida set, please.

4
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:19,268
Where were you, Minami? Dressed like that?

5
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,895
Our morning meeting was canceled,

6
00:00:21,896 --> 00:00:23,939
so there's no point going in early.

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,774
So I went for a run.

8
00:00:25,775 --> 00:00:26,817
Right.

9
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:30,070
So you haven't abandoned work again.

10
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:31,906
I haven't quit quitting quitting!

11
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:34,616
To prepare for my next case,

12
00:00:34,617 --> 00:00:36,452
I've been building stamina!

13
00:00:36,453 --> 00:00:38,329
You're certainly motivated.

14
00:00:39,122 --> 00:00:41,999
Your managing partner

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,169
praised you on the phone the other day.

16
00:00:44,878 --> 00:00:45,711
Managing Partner?

17
00:00:45,712 --> 00:00:47,672
Persistent and creative, she said.

18
00:00:50,592 --> 00:00:53,219
Why were you on the phone
with the managing partner?

19
00:00:55,013 --> 00:00:57,056
Hirokawa & Howard LPC

20
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:59,434
has 712 lawyers.

21
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:03,063
Why would she speak to a rookie's father?

22
00:01:04,064 --> 00:01:05,189
Well...

23
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:06,566
You see...

24
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:10,027
I couldn't reach you on your phone,

25
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:11,570
so I called the firm.

26
00:01:11,571 --> 00:01:12,739
She happened to answer.

27
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:15,240
- Happened to?
- Yes.

28
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:16,909
- Answer?
- Yes.

29
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,119
Managing Partner?

30
00:01:20,121 --> 00:01:24,374
Maybe her secretary was out at lunch.

31
00:01:24,375 --> 00:01:26,795
It was around lunchtime.

32
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:30,215
That's right.

33
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:33,343
Your phone! Answer it. Go on.

34
00:01:40,725 --> 00:01:41,600
Hello?

35
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:44,354
Morning, Ms. Minamida. Where are you?

36
00:01:44,896 --> 00:01:45,854
At home.

37
00:01:45,855 --> 00:01:47,856
What about the briefing?

38
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:50,734
Today's meeting was moved to tomorrow.

39
00:01:50,735 --> 00:01:52,736
Mr. Himi told me.

40
00:01:52,737 --> 00:01:55,697
Yes, the meeting was canceled

41
00:01:55,698 --> 00:01:57,826
- because today...
- Morning.

42
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:01,120
Because a client visit came up
at short notice today.

43
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:03,331
We need a briefing beforehand.

44
00:02:04,791 --> 00:02:06,167
A briefing?

45
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:09,253
Come in.

46
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:10,421
Excuse me!

47
00:02:16,636 --> 00:02:18,011
Good morning!

48
00:02:18,012 --> 00:02:19,096
That outfit?

49
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,222
I came in a rush.

50
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,390
You ran here?

51
00:02:21,391 --> 00:02:24,101
Yes! I thought I had time this morning,

52
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:25,561
so I went running.

53
00:02:25,562 --> 00:02:27,938
I'm not sure I follow,

54
00:02:27,939 --> 00:02:30,024
but leave yourself more time.

55
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,402
I'm sorry.

56
00:02:34,612 --> 00:02:35,946
Mr. Himi.

57
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:38,991
Why didn't you tell me about the briefing?

58
00:02:38,992 --> 00:02:40,367
I thought I did.

59
00:02:40,368 --> 00:02:42,077
You only mentioned the meeting.

60
00:02:42,078 --> 00:02:44,121
Maybe you weren't listening.

61
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:46,166
All right. We're short on time.

62
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,333
But Mr. Himi...

63
00:02:48,334 --> 00:02:51,169
Fine, let's leave it at that. Mr. Miyaji.

64
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,754
Her documents, please.

65
00:02:52,755 --> 00:02:54,214
I'll give her a copy.

66
00:02:54,215 --> 00:02:55,592
Here you are.

67
00:02:59,762 --> 00:03:01,638
- I'll read them quickly.
- No need.

68
00:03:01,639 --> 00:03:03,015
I'll explain briefly.

69
00:03:03,016 --> 00:03:05,476
Yes. Briefly, please.

70
00:03:08,271 --> 00:03:11,900
Our client is a major school,
Ray Arrows Dance Academy.

71
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:19,114
The other party runs a dance school too.

72
00:03:19,115 --> 00:03:21,034
Saty, a dancer and choreographer.

73
00:03:22,076 --> 00:03:25,495
<i>She used to be
Ray Arrows' star instructor.</i>

74
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:26,747
<i>She went independent</i>

75
00:03:26,748 --> 00:03:28,248
<i>and in August,</i>

76
00:03:28,249 --> 00:03:31,044
<i>opened Fordee Dance Studio.</i>

77
00:03:31,711 --> 00:03:34,379
She choreographs for pop idols,

78
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,632
so she has some influence.

79
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:39,760
She posted criticism of Ray Arrows online.

80
00:03:39,761 --> 00:03:40,761
SATY

81
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:45,557
"Great times. 'Pro' teachers thrive
just teaching the motions. ()"

82
00:03:45,558 --> 00:03:48,393
"It'd be interesting to require
all instructors to be licensed."

83
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:52,940
Those empty parentheses are slang.
There's no "laugh" inside.

84
00:03:52,941 --> 00:03:55,192
It's sarcastic, "Not funny."

85
00:03:55,193 --> 00:03:58,320
They see it as defamation
and business interference

86
00:03:58,321 --> 00:04:01,949
and want to sue Saty for damages.

87
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,910
The client will be here shortly.

88
00:04:04,911 --> 00:04:07,537
Details then. I already told Mr. Himi,

89
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:11,500
but you'll both be handling this case,
Ms. Minamida.

90
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:12,501
And you?

91
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:14,670
I'm busy with another matter.

92
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,588
Medical Association head Watagami, right?

93
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:18,632
In that case,
you can leave this one just to me.

94
00:04:18,633 --> 00:04:20,425
What? I'm doing it too!

95
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:21,927
Then I'll leave it to you both.

96
00:04:21,928 --> 00:04:23,137
- Yes!
- Yes!

97
00:04:33,898 --> 00:04:36,358
That Saty woman exaggerates

98
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,486
to make herself look good.

99
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:40,237
Even winning that contest,

100
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:43,031
she takes all the credit for it,

101
00:04:43,032 --> 00:04:46,451
but she just did exactly what I advised.

102
00:04:46,452 --> 00:04:49,580
Really? So you were behind it, Chairman!

103
00:04:50,456 --> 00:04:53,167
Are you a professional dancer, then?

104
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,043
What?

105
00:04:55,044 --> 00:04:57,838
Or, as Saty put it in her post,

106
00:04:57,839 --> 00:04:59,215
are you a self-proclaimed pro?

107
00:05:01,175 --> 00:05:02,135
Who is she?

108
00:05:03,553 --> 00:05:06,264
All our instructors
are teaching professionals.

109
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:09,934
Then "self-proclaimed" is insulting.

110
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:13,228
To teach her a lesson in life,

111
00:05:13,229 --> 00:05:15,856
I say we make her pay a fortune.

112
00:05:15,857 --> 00:05:18,776
Agreed. Let's make her pay a fortune.

113
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:24,032
But establishing defamation
from this would be difficult.

114
00:05:24,657 --> 00:05:25,824
Even if we do,

115
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:28,285
damages are usually
a few hundred thousand yen.

116
00:05:28,286 --> 00:05:29,870
Hardly a fortune.

117
00:05:29,871 --> 00:05:34,291
Those posts damaged our school's brand.

118
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:35,667
That's a fact.

119
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:37,919
You want me to just take it?

120
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,089
No, that's not what I mean...

121
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:42,090
Chairman.

122
00:05:42,091 --> 00:05:44,551
To establish defamation

123
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,636
and increase the damages,

124
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:50,390
I searched Saty's old posts for anything

125
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:52,685
that could be criticism of Ray Arrows.

126
00:05:53,561 --> 00:05:56,189
You investigated all of this?

127
00:05:56,689 --> 00:05:57,981
Yes. On my own.

128
00:05:57,982 --> 00:06:00,901
I wanted to be as prepared as possible.

129
00:06:00,902 --> 00:06:03,529
Just what I'd expect from a top firm.

130
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:08,075
Mr. Himi.

131
00:06:08,076 --> 00:06:09,159
Yes?

132
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,494
Very reassuring.

133
00:06:10,495 --> 00:06:11,871
You're too kind.

134
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,084
Here's one I found.

135
00:06:17,085 --> 00:06:20,712
"Classes are too big.
Students at all different levels."

136
00:06:20,713 --> 00:06:22,548
"Will you ever group them properly?"

137
00:06:23,758 --> 00:06:25,967
"Work hard. Get treated the same."

138
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:29,430
"The best people keep leaving."
There's more.

139
00:06:32,725 --> 00:06:35,685
Let's prove these posts are baseless!

140
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:37,771
Yes. I'm counting on you.

141
00:06:37,772 --> 00:06:42,275
Of course. First, I'd like to speak
with your staff.

142
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:45,904
I'm driving back to the school.
Want to come?

143
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:48,240
May I? Thank you.

144
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,407
I'll come too!

145
00:06:49,408 --> 00:06:50,867
I can do the interviews alone.

146
00:06:50,868 --> 00:06:51,868
But...

147
00:06:51,869 --> 00:06:53,370
I'll be right behind you.

148
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,955
- See you shortly.
- Yes.

149
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:55,956
Mr. Himi...

150
00:06:55,957 --> 00:06:57,041
Thank you.

151
00:07:06,759 --> 00:07:07,592
Mr. Himi.

152
00:07:07,593 --> 00:07:10,429
Not seeing the documents
beforehand put me at a disadvantage.

153
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:12,890
Please share what you learn.

154
00:07:14,684 --> 00:07:15,518
I'd rather not.

155
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:17,727
Rather not?

156
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:21,441
This case came
through a major client's referral.

157
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:24,235
I need to score some points.

158
00:07:25,695 --> 00:07:29,240
You don't need to do
anything this time. Bye.

159
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:36,581
What now?

160
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:42,128
I won't be outdone.

161
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:56,349
Are you sure it's okay
to come here uninvited?

162
00:07:56,350 --> 00:07:57,643
It's not a problem.

163
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:02,898
We need to see if the person
we're suing really would slander others.

164
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:05,902
Looking into her character
should give us a lead.

165
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,491
CONSTRUCTION
WATCH FOR TRUCKS

166
00:08:12,492 --> 00:08:15,243
Fordee Dance Studio
is behind this hospital.

167
00:08:15,244 --> 00:08:16,746
WATAGAMI HOSPITAL

168
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:23,336
Are you okay?

169
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:29,050
I'm fine. Just startled.

170
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:31,093
Let's go!

171
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,262
Let's go.

172
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:37,349
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO

173
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,559
Hey! Going to class?

174
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,645
Yeah. Bye!

175
00:08:47,151 --> 00:08:50,195
Are all these cars picking up children

176
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,989
from Fordee Dance Studio?

177
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,658
It's really popular.

178
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,160
Yuma! Yuma!

179
00:08:56,994 --> 00:08:58,955
- You forgot this.
- Thanks.

180
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,918
Excuse me.
Are you dropping off your child?

181
00:09:04,710 --> 00:09:07,087
Oh, my car? I'll move it right away.

182
00:09:07,088 --> 00:09:08,129
No.

183
00:09:08,130 --> 00:09:11,217
We're thinking of dance lessons
for our child.

184
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:18,182
What's Ms. Saty like as a teacher?

185
00:09:18,849 --> 00:09:22,311
Does she exaggerate or take
credit for others' work?

186
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,896
I don't think so.

187
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:26,064
She's a good teacher.

188
00:09:26,065 --> 00:09:28,108
And an amazing dancer.

189
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:30,819
Want to watch a lesson?

190
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,446
ENROLL NOW! COME WATCH A CLASS

191
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:55,469
This is more than a hobby class.

192
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:59,056
Go, go, go! Push harder!

193
00:10:05,521 --> 00:10:06,981
Finish strong!

194
00:10:08,441 --> 00:10:10,651
Yeah! That's good!

195
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:12,611
Yuma, you fell behind.

196
00:10:12,612 --> 00:10:13,612
- So close.
- Yes.

197
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,447
The rest was great, though.

198
00:10:15,448 --> 00:10:17,283
You're all geniuses!

199
00:10:18,326 --> 00:10:19,951
Five-minute break!

200
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:20,911
Yes!

201
00:10:28,085 --> 00:10:30,629
- Was that helpful?
- Yes!

202
00:10:30,630 --> 00:10:33,340
You were all so perfectly in sync!

203
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:35,676
We represent the school, after all.

204
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,847
We're entering this contest next month.

205
00:10:40,848 --> 00:10:44,185
Ms. Saty's class won it last year, right?

206
00:10:45,353 --> 00:10:47,438
We're aiming to win too.

207
00:10:50,024 --> 00:10:51,984
With that dance just now?

208
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,529
With moves like this.

209
00:10:56,197 --> 00:10:58,157
That's quite an original take.

210
00:10:58,616 --> 00:10:59,742
Like this, right?

211
00:11:02,620 --> 00:11:04,788
Yes! Exactly! That's it.

212
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:06,039
You're very good.

213
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:07,291
Want to try it with us?

214
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,711
- Yes, please!
- What?

215
00:11:21,347 --> 00:11:22,972
Again!

216
00:11:22,973 --> 00:11:26,143
Hey! No adding members without asking!

217
00:11:27,645 --> 00:11:30,064
Sorry.

218
00:11:30,898 --> 00:11:32,566
Lessons for your child?

219
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:34,484
Yes...

220
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:36,653
They're all so good.

221
00:11:36,654 --> 00:11:38,071
Are they aiming to go pro?

222
00:11:38,072 --> 00:11:39,656
Some want to.

223
00:11:39,657 --> 00:11:42,992
But even if they don't go pro,

224
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:45,413
lessons should give them lasting skills.

225
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:47,623
Lasting skills?

226
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,583
Some schools don't even teach the basics.

227
00:11:50,584 --> 00:11:52,961
They just have kids move to music.

228
00:11:52,962 --> 00:11:54,755
There are plenty of schools like that.

229
00:11:55,506 --> 00:11:59,342
I want children to learn real dance.

230
00:11:59,343 --> 00:12:00,970
That's why I opened this.

231
00:12:02,763 --> 00:12:04,556
She seems like a good teacher.

232
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,558
Yes, a good teacher.

233
00:12:06,559 --> 00:12:08,643
No rush to join.

234
00:12:08,644 --> 00:12:09,978
Visit other schools

235
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:11,897
and choose what suits your child.

236
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,860
Let's visit Ray Arrows too.

237
00:12:16,861 --> 00:12:18,487
They're famous too.

238
00:12:20,239 --> 00:12:22,408
I don't mean to interfere,

239
00:12:23,033 --> 00:12:26,036
but being famous
doesn't make a school good.

240
00:12:29,957 --> 00:12:32,709
Break's over. Let's pick up
where we left off.

241
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,419
- Yes!
- Line up.

242
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:37,882
Unbelievable. You should've told me
before going undercover.

243
00:12:41,051 --> 00:12:41,969
Well?

244
00:12:42,470 --> 00:12:44,138
Did you learn anything?

245
00:12:45,556 --> 00:12:49,601
Saty was quite unlike
our client's description.

246
00:12:49,602 --> 00:12:51,644
Students and parents love her.

247
00:12:51,645 --> 00:12:54,397
They all said she's a good teacher.

248
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:58,527
They're customers.
Of course she'd be nice to them.

249
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:03,907
Tell me what your interviews revealed.

250
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:06,951
No. You didn't bring me anything useful,

251
00:13:06,952 --> 00:13:08,411
so it's hardly a fair trade.

252
00:13:08,412 --> 00:13:10,914
I need you to share your findings.

253
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:15,168
Or did no one confirm
that the posts were false?

254
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,378
Someone did.

255
00:13:18,881 --> 00:13:20,758
Then share it with me.

256
00:13:21,884 --> 00:13:24,886
Ray Arrows may be hiding the truth

257
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:28,015
and using a lawsuit to silence Saty.

258
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:30,851
You think this is a SLAPP suit?

259
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:34,229
I'm saying it's a possibility.

260
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:36,606
No, that's not possible.

261
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:37,816
Why not?

262
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:41,611
A SLAPP is when a wealthy party

263
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:45,240
drags out a case against someone poorer

264
00:13:45,241 --> 00:13:48,826
to wear them down and silence criticism.

265
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:51,747
But how big are these two schools?

266
00:13:52,456 --> 00:13:54,249
- About the same.
- Right.

267
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:58,878
If this drags on, wouldn't Ray Arrows
face the same financial burden?

268
00:13:58,879 --> 00:13:59,796
Yes.

269
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,297
Exactly.

270
00:14:01,298 --> 00:14:05,843
Even if they hate her,
that wouldn't be cost-effective.

271
00:14:05,844 --> 00:14:07,638
That's true, but...

272
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:11,976
Trust the client who wants to proceed.

273
00:14:12,893 --> 00:14:15,604
Isn't that our duty as lawyers?

274
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,358
Understood.

275
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:22,611
No objections to proceeding, then?

276
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,954
Among elite dancers,

277
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:36,040
rivals are valued
for pushing each other to improve.

278
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:37,126
FIRST ORAL ARGUMENT

279
00:14:37,710 --> 00:14:41,088
The defendant's posts
merely offer such encouragement.

280
00:14:41,672 --> 00:14:44,257
They don't damage anyone's reputation.

281
00:14:44,258 --> 00:14:45,758
Objection! On that point...

282
00:14:45,759 --> 00:14:47,260
- Case law...
- Objection!

283
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,304
Plaintiff's counsel!

284
00:14:48,888 --> 00:14:50,848
One at a time, please.

285
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:55,102
I'll speak.

286
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:03,484
Defamation depends on how
the audience perceives it.

287
00:15:03,485 --> 00:15:04,444
The post says,

288
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:08,114
"Great times. 'Pro' teachers thrive
just teaching the motions."

289
00:15:08,115 --> 00:15:10,575
The empty parentheses at the end

290
00:15:10,576 --> 00:15:13,036
are common slang with no "laugh" inside.

291
00:15:13,037 --> 00:15:15,788
a sarcastic way of saying "not funny."

292
00:15:15,789 --> 00:15:19,042
Most readers wouldn't interpret
that as encouragement.

293
00:15:19,043 --> 00:15:20,668
I would also add

294
00:15:20,669 --> 00:15:23,338
she has over 100,000 followers.

295
00:15:23,339 --> 00:15:26,758
Before today's hearing,
it had over four million views,

296
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:29,135
11,000 likes, and reposts...

297
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,553
3,421!

298
00:15:30,554 --> 00:15:32,513
3,421 reposts.

299
00:15:32,514 --> 00:15:36,392
Saty's influence
in the dance world is considerable!

300
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,310
It is!

301
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,854
Plaintiff's counsel.

302
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:41,941
Only one of you may speak.

303
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,278
Sorry.

304
00:15:47,655 --> 00:15:49,530
In light of this,

305
00:15:49,531 --> 00:15:53,243
we believe
this post constitutes defamation.

306
00:16:00,793 --> 00:16:02,461
So you're lawyers.

307
00:16:05,005 --> 00:16:07,966
I don't appreciate being
investigated like that.

308
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,385
Many of our students are young children.

309
00:16:10,386 --> 00:16:12,762
Please take that into account.

310
00:16:12,763 --> 00:16:14,347
I'm sorry.

311
00:16:14,348 --> 00:16:15,473
Sorry.

312
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:16,432
Besides,

313
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:18,977
what's the point of this lawsuit?

314
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:22,522
Right before a major competition,
you sue us?

315
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,065
That's pure harassment.

316
00:16:24,066 --> 00:16:25,858
You're the one harassing us!

317
00:16:25,859 --> 00:16:28,987
Smearing us with your false posts.

318
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,655
I only wrote the truth.

319
00:16:30,656 --> 00:16:32,365
What truth?

320
00:16:32,366 --> 00:16:35,618
- You've started rumors!
- They're worse than us.

321
00:16:35,619 --> 00:16:37,745
Aren't you the one lying?

322
00:16:37,746 --> 00:16:38,955
That contest win,

323
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:41,541
I hear you've been taking credit for it.

324
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,334
Have you ever danced?

325
00:16:43,335 --> 00:16:46,462
I'd never say such a thing.

326
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:48,965
- I heard you did.
- He did say it, right?

327
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:51,342
- You believed him?
- What?

328
00:16:51,343 --> 00:16:54,053
Mr. Himi, you knew he was lying?

329
00:16:54,054 --> 00:16:56,931
You said our duty was to trust clients.

330
00:16:56,932 --> 00:17:00,936
I'll fight to the bitter end,
however long it takes!

331
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:07,234
Lying is wrong!

332
00:17:07,943 --> 00:17:11,112
Mr. Himi, any other lies? Please tell me.

333
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:14,533
Well... Not about the lawsuit, I think.

334
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,087
This one?

335
00:17:29,089 --> 00:17:30,549
This one?

336
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:34,093
You two!

337
00:17:34,094 --> 00:17:36,680
Clear some plates if you're just playing.

338
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:38,431
We're not playing.

339
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:40,267
We're practicing spotting lies.

340
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:43,395
Spotting lies? Playing Old Maid?

341
00:17:43,854 --> 00:17:45,271
Minami, the eyes.

342
00:17:45,272 --> 00:17:47,316
The eyes will usually give them away.

343
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,538
I still can't tell.

344
00:18:02,372 --> 00:18:06,000
Autistic people struggle to read
expressions through eye contact.

345
00:18:06,001 --> 00:18:08,294
Minami, try the nose instead.

346
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:09,587
The nose?

347
00:18:09,588 --> 00:18:13,216
They say lying releases catecholamines,

348
00:18:13,217 --> 00:18:16,427
which swell the tissue in
your nose and make it itch.

349
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,054
- The joker!
- Listening?

350
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:21,100
I've never seen anyone's nose
swell or itch from lying.

351
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:23,352
Pinocchio's grows.

352
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:34,947
I win! Minami, you're terrible!

353
00:18:36,031 --> 00:18:37,657
How can you tell, Ririi?

354
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,242
You're easy to read.

355
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:40,493
Say something.

356
00:18:40,494 --> 00:18:41,954
I'll guess if it's a lie.

357
00:18:44,123 --> 00:18:45,207
Then...

358
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:49,544
I don't want to lose to Mr. Himi.

359
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,837
Mr. Himi? Who's that?

360
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,923
We're working on a case together.

361
00:18:53,632 --> 00:18:56,384
But he won't share information,

362
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,387
and I doubt he's investigated properly.

363
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:02,932
So I'll have to redo
the interviews tomorrow.

364
00:19:02,933 --> 00:19:04,809
I wouldn't want to lose to him.

365
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,394
True or false?

366
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:07,937
It's probably...

367
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:09,522
True! That's true!

368
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:11,315
Hey! Don't answer for me!

369
00:19:11,316 --> 00:19:13,442
Ririi and I are practicing.

370
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:14,945
Please go away, Dad.

371
00:19:15,821 --> 00:19:17,072
Come on.

372
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,740
Let's switch.

373
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:22,452
You guess whether what I say
is true or false.

374
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:24,288
Okay.

375
00:19:29,543 --> 00:19:31,170
Minato Funai...

376
00:19:32,754 --> 00:19:35,173
likes Minami Minamida.

377
00:19:35,174 --> 00:19:36,633
Romantically.

378
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:42,180
What's that?

379
00:19:42,181 --> 00:19:43,473
You two watched the sunset.

380
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:45,726
Yes.

381
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:51,064
Ririi, do you know the answer?

382
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:52,900
Well, yes.

383
00:19:53,775 --> 00:19:54,609
Tell me.

384
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:55,985
That defeats the point.

385
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,737
Tell me!

386
00:19:57,738 --> 00:19:58,988
Not telling!

387
00:19:58,989 --> 00:19:59,906
Tell me!

388
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,449
Come on, let's play again. Clear up.

389
00:20:01,450 --> 00:20:02,618
Ririi, tell me.

390
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:09,373
MINAMI MINAMIDA

391
00:20:09,374 --> 00:20:11,250
<i>Before we visit Ray Arrows tomorrow,</i>

392
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:13,128
<i>I have a question.</i>

393
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:16,798
<i>A question?</i>

394
00:20:17,341 --> 00:20:18,383
<i>Of course.</i>

395
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,094
<i>Is it about work?</i>

396
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,182
<i>Or about whales?</i>

397
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,103
Your girlfriend?

398
00:20:31,104 --> 00:20:33,231
No, it's not.

399
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:35,233
You look happy.

400
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,525
Making plans for a date?

401
00:20:36,526 --> 00:20:37,903
It's about work.

402
00:20:38,612 --> 00:20:39,947
You crossed your arms.

403
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:41,740
So?

404
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:45,743
A detective I know told me

405
00:20:45,744 --> 00:20:47,620
when people lie,

406
00:20:47,621 --> 00:20:49,497
they don't want to get caught.

407
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:52,084
Their urge to protect themselves grows.

408
00:20:52,793 --> 00:20:55,711
That state of mind makes them

409
00:20:55,712 --> 00:20:59,424
cross their arms to form
a physical barrier.

410
00:21:02,803 --> 00:21:04,596
Or cross their legs.

411
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:08,849
You're popular with women.

412
00:21:08,850 --> 00:21:11,228
Don't let the other women here find out.

413
00:21:12,396 --> 00:21:13,938
Who is it?

414
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,691
Someone here? A lawyer?

415
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,775
No, it's nothing like that.

416
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:19,318
Just administrative work.

417
00:21:19,319 --> 00:21:21,862
Now you're covering your mouth.

418
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:23,490
What? This too?

419
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:33,834
<i>I have a question
before we visit Ray Arrows.</i>

420
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,137
Good morning.

421
00:21:45,762 --> 00:21:47,014
Good morning.

422
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,725
Shall we go, then?

423
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:53,312
Yes.

424
00:21:54,730 --> 00:21:57,898
A detective
who's a friend of a friend said

425
00:21:57,899 --> 00:22:00,276
people cross their arms

426
00:22:00,277 --> 00:22:02,446
or legs when they're lying.

427
00:22:04,239 --> 00:22:06,532
Cross their arms and legs?

428
00:22:06,533 --> 00:22:09,410
Yes. I think it's fairly accurate.

429
00:22:09,411 --> 00:22:11,579
And putting a hand over your mouth

430
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:14,041
apparently means you want to hide a lie.

431
00:22:16,209 --> 00:22:17,626
Ririi said eyes.

432
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:20,046
Dad said to watch the nose.

433
00:22:20,047 --> 00:22:23,090
So I have to watch eyes, noses, mouths,

434
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:26,094
and the whole body at once?

435
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:28,930
That's very difficult.

436
00:22:39,357 --> 00:22:41,026
About what I just said,

437
00:22:41,860 --> 00:22:43,736
don't get too caught up in it.

438
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:46,073
Maybe just talk as you normally would.

439
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:48,283
Trust your instincts.

440
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,829
My instincts are often wrong.

441
00:22:53,747 --> 00:22:55,332
Many autistic people

442
00:22:55,832 --> 00:22:58,293
are easily deceived and can't lie.

443
00:22:59,086 --> 00:23:00,212
I'm one of them.

444
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:04,131
If being fooled were a competition,

445
00:23:04,132 --> 00:23:05,801
I'd make the podium.

446
00:23:07,803 --> 00:23:11,807
Because autistic people are more innocent?

447
00:23:14,518 --> 00:23:16,520
Not so much innocent...

448
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,732
Most people

449
00:23:21,274 --> 00:23:24,069
live in a world with
themselves and others.

450
00:23:25,028 --> 00:23:26,238
But autistic people

451
00:23:26,863 --> 00:23:29,157
live in a world of their own.

452
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:31,868
I think that's why.

453
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:36,540
A world of their own?

454
00:23:37,582 --> 00:23:38,542
Yes.

455
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:42,671
I know people think differently from me

456
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:45,506
and might deceive me.

457
00:23:45,507 --> 00:23:48,510
But even knowing that, I forget.

458
00:23:49,219 --> 00:23:52,263
In today's interviews, for instance,

459
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:54,056
the Ray Arrows staff

460
00:23:54,057 --> 00:23:57,102
may lie to please the chairman.

461
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:59,770
To avoid being deceived,

462
00:23:59,771 --> 00:24:02,816
I have to keep thinking,
"Don't be fooled."

463
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:04,985
I have to stay conscious of it.

464
00:24:06,987 --> 00:24:08,655
That's helpful to know.

465
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:12,159
It helps?

466
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:13,826
I mean...

467
00:24:13,827 --> 00:24:17,706
It's very helpful for understanding you.

468
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:22,252
In that sense, it is helpful.

469
00:24:33,555 --> 00:24:35,515
Taking a break, Mr. Himi?

470
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:39,561
Ms. Minamida and Mr. Funai
went to see the client.

471
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:42,480
There they go meddling again.

472
00:24:43,565 --> 00:24:45,900
More importantly, Ms. Asahi, are you okay

473
00:24:45,901 --> 00:24:48,069
with Funai and Minamida being together?

474
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:50,738
What?

475
00:24:50,739 --> 00:24:53,241
You know, office romance.

476
00:24:53,992 --> 00:24:57,329
When people spend time
together, it can happen.

477
00:24:57,996 --> 00:25:00,665
Then again, Ms. Minamida's no threat.

478
00:25:02,334 --> 00:25:04,586
You must have a lot of free time.

479
00:25:05,503 --> 00:25:08,173
I'm only saying this to support you.

480
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:11,592
What?

481
00:25:11,593 --> 00:25:15,012
The person Funai likes...

482
00:25:15,013 --> 00:25:18,432
I think it might be you, Ms. Asahi.

483
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:20,100
What?

484
00:25:20,101 --> 00:25:22,062
Did Mr. Funai say something?

485
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:24,688
About me? To you?

486
00:25:24,689 --> 00:25:26,024
Curious?

487
00:25:29,694 --> 00:25:30,904
No, no...

488
00:25:31,821 --> 00:25:32,948
Not really.

489
00:25:39,496 --> 00:25:41,997
Shall we practice, then?

490
00:25:41,998 --> 00:25:45,585
Ask me questions
as if I work at Ray Arrows.

491
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:47,879
Understood.

492
00:25:51,883 --> 00:25:54,761
Look into my eyes, please.

493
00:26:00,475 --> 00:26:02,102
Ask me anything.

494
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:06,398
Here goes.

495
00:26:09,150 --> 00:26:12,152
Minato Funai likes Minami Minamida.

496
00:26:12,153 --> 00:26:13,613
Is that true?

497
00:26:15,115 --> 00:26:16,199
What?

498
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:19,577
Is it true or false?

499
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:32,299
Well...

500
00:26:40,890 --> 00:26:42,726
For a member of staff,

501
00:26:43,893 --> 00:26:45,729
that's a difficult question.

502
00:26:51,776 --> 00:26:52,819
That's right.

503
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:55,780
This is interview practice.

504
00:27:09,336 --> 00:27:11,963
Class sizes are like this everywhere.

505
00:27:12,839 --> 00:27:13,923
The mouth...

506
00:27:16,634 --> 00:27:19,763
Depends how particular you want to be.

507
00:27:20,430 --> 00:27:21,389
The arms?

508
00:27:24,517 --> 00:27:25,642
Right.

509
00:27:25,643 --> 00:27:28,104
Ms. Saty's on a different level from us.

510
00:27:28,938 --> 00:27:30,065
Nose and eyes?

511
00:27:36,863 --> 00:27:39,698
And how are you treated here?

512
00:27:39,699 --> 00:27:41,701
Well, it's not really about that...

513
00:27:45,163 --> 00:27:47,122
Please let me see your face.

514
00:27:47,123 --> 00:27:49,166
Hello, everyone.

515
00:27:49,167 --> 00:27:50,417
Hello.

516
00:27:50,418 --> 00:27:51,377
A treat.

517
00:27:51,378 --> 00:27:54,463
Sometimes we get those special tarts.

518
00:27:54,464 --> 00:27:55,589
It's a nice perk.

519
00:27:55,590 --> 00:27:57,759
Here we go! Ta-da!

520
00:27:59,260 --> 00:28:01,428
This one looks the best.

521
00:28:01,429 --> 00:28:02,721
It's huge!

522
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:04,139
Wow. Which one?

523
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:06,517
Can I have this one?

524
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:08,435
Everyone, stop.

525
00:28:08,436 --> 00:28:10,854
You crossed your arms and legs.

526
00:28:10,855 --> 00:28:12,816
What are you all hiding?

527
00:28:19,114 --> 00:28:23,451
I hoped to find at least
one more clue than Mr. Himi.

528
00:28:24,869 --> 00:28:27,246
But I have to wonder,

529
00:28:27,247 --> 00:28:30,207
is this really worth suing over?

530
00:28:30,208 --> 00:28:32,167
Saty has her approach.

531
00:28:32,168 --> 00:28:36,631
Ray Arrows has theirs.
Isn't that all it is?

532
00:28:44,013 --> 00:28:44,848
Ms. Minamida?

533
00:28:46,599 --> 00:28:47,976
Those orange shoes.

534
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:50,812
Yuma and his friends wore them too.

535
00:28:51,604 --> 00:28:53,230
These are specially designed, right?

536
00:28:53,231 --> 00:28:56,818
They had the same little
smiley face on theirs.

537
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:02,741
We all used to be students here.

538
00:29:03,324 --> 00:29:06,369
We were in Ms. Saty's class,
aiming for the competition.

539
00:29:07,036 --> 00:29:10,039
We got matching shoes before entering.

540
00:29:11,416 --> 00:29:13,042
Only you stayed?

541
00:29:14,335 --> 00:29:17,130
I wanted to keep studying here.

542
00:29:18,965 --> 00:29:21,384
But you even got matching shoes.

543
00:29:21,885 --> 00:29:24,637
Didn't you want to compete alongside them?

544
00:29:25,638 --> 00:29:26,514
Not really...

545
00:29:27,015 --> 00:29:28,475
Competitions, I...

546
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:30,351
I'm not interested.

547
00:29:35,106 --> 00:29:36,148
Her mouth...

548
00:29:36,149 --> 00:29:37,400
She touched it.

549
00:30:04,552 --> 00:30:06,762
What did you want to discuss?

550
00:30:06,763 --> 00:30:07,805
Yes.

551
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:11,975
Regarding the civil suit
against Fordee Dance Studio,

552
00:30:11,976 --> 00:30:13,520
I suggest withdrawing it.

553
00:30:13,978 --> 00:30:17,314
What? You want to give up?

554
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:19,316
I'm not dropping the lawsuit.

555
00:30:19,317 --> 00:30:20,275
Yes.

556
00:30:20,276 --> 00:30:25,864
We'll drop the defamation claim
for damages against Saty

557
00:30:25,865 --> 00:30:28,534
and sue Fordee Dance Studio instead

558
00:30:28,535 --> 00:30:30,786
in a new lawsuit.

559
00:30:30,787 --> 00:30:33,248
Why go to all that trouble?

560
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:38,377
You just resent me taking
the lead on this case, don't you?

561
00:30:38,378 --> 00:30:40,170
That's not true.

562
00:30:40,171 --> 00:30:44,007
I've found a more reliable way
to secure damages.

563
00:30:44,008 --> 00:30:45,593
- Chairman.
- Well...

564
00:30:47,053 --> 00:30:48,263
Let's hear her out.

565
00:30:51,808 --> 00:30:54,018
Minato, your help, please.

566
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:12,786
We focused only on what Saty's posts said.

567
00:31:12,787 --> 00:31:15,290
We should've looked at the dates.

568
00:31:16,916 --> 00:31:20,545
Saty left Ray Arrows on June 30.

569
00:31:27,385 --> 00:31:28,552
RAY ARROWS
JUNE - SATY RESIGNS

570
00:31:28,553 --> 00:31:31,930
Yes. Her contract ran through June.

571
00:31:31,931 --> 00:31:34,850
And Fordee Dance Studio

572
00:31:34,851 --> 00:31:37,312
opened on August 1st.

573
00:31:38,521 --> 00:31:40,147
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO OPEN - 14 TRANSFERS

574
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:43,902
They're now training
for next month's competition.

575
00:31:46,195 --> 00:31:48,155
RAY ARROWS SEP - 397, 21 LEFT
OCT - 342, 34 LEFT

576
00:31:48,156 --> 00:31:52,618
The unit representing
Fordee Dance Studio at the competition,

577
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,244
Team Nikori,

578
00:31:54,245 --> 00:31:57,623
is made up entirely of former
Ray Arrows students.

579
00:31:57,624 --> 00:32:00,167
A photo of them in matching shoes

580
00:32:00,168 --> 00:32:02,879
was posted on June 1st.

581
00:32:06,758 --> 00:32:07,966
JUNE, JULY, AUGUST...

582
00:32:07,967 --> 00:32:12,263
So when did Saty
enter them in the competition?

583
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:15,974
I contacted the organizers.

584
00:32:15,975 --> 00:32:18,560
They said that, as of June 10,

585
00:32:18,561 --> 00:32:21,856
Team Nikori was already
entered under Fordee Dance Studio.

586
00:32:22,732 --> 00:32:23,982
June?

587
00:32:23,983 --> 00:32:25,610
She was still under contract to us.

588
00:32:26,694 --> 00:32:31,823
I reviewed the employment contract
between Saty and Ray Arrows.

589
00:32:31,824 --> 00:32:35,118
It states that if she sets up
a competing business,

590
00:32:35,119 --> 00:32:37,705
she may not poach their clients.

591
00:32:38,498 --> 00:32:41,500
In other words,
Saty's actions constitute poaching

592
00:32:41,501 --> 00:32:42,961
and appear to breach her contract.

593
00:32:43,795 --> 00:32:45,671
Now I see!

594
00:32:45,672 --> 00:32:46,922
As a result,

595
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:49,633
Ray Arrows not only lost students,

596
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:52,970
but a valuable publicity opportunity
at the competition,

597
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:56,474
and potentially
a chance to recruit new students.

598
00:32:57,058 --> 00:32:58,183
The resulting losses

599
00:32:58,184 --> 00:33:02,688
likely exceed the damages
claimed for defamation.

600
00:33:02,689 --> 00:33:05,900
This could really hurt her.

601
00:33:07,276 --> 00:33:08,819
Ms. Minami Minamida,

602
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:11,029
I'm going with your plan!

603
00:33:11,030 --> 00:33:13,573
Then keep the defamation claim

604
00:33:13,574 --> 00:33:15,450
and just add breach of contract...

605
00:33:15,451 --> 00:33:16,827
Then, Mr. Himi,

606
00:33:16,828 --> 00:33:21,207
did you obtain any testimony
proving that her posts were false?

607
00:33:22,250 --> 00:33:23,334
Well...

608
00:33:23,918 --> 00:33:25,919
Then we'll withdraw

609
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:29,589
the defamation damages claim against Saty

610
00:33:29,590 --> 00:33:31,883
and file a new claim

611
00:33:31,884 --> 00:33:34,845
for damages for breach of contract.

612
00:33:34,846 --> 00:33:36,597
Any objections?

613
00:33:47,066 --> 00:33:48,192
This way.

614
00:33:50,737 --> 00:33:52,696
Hello.

615
00:33:52,697 --> 00:33:54,489
She works under me.

616
00:33:54,490 --> 00:33:58,453
My client, Mr. Watagami,
Medical Association president.

617
00:33:59,203 --> 00:34:00,246
I'm Minami Minamida.

618
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:03,582
Forwards or backwards, Minami Minamida.

619
00:34:03,583 --> 00:34:06,669
Kayak, deed, rotator,
civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

620
00:34:07,545 --> 00:34:08,588
She's interesting.

621
00:34:09,297 --> 00:34:11,089
Is she handling the Ray Arrows case?

622
00:34:11,090 --> 00:34:12,216
Yes.

623
00:34:13,134 --> 00:34:16,261
Yes. I'm handling that case.

624
00:34:16,262 --> 00:34:19,598
I heard you're withdrawing one suit
to file another.

625
00:34:19,599 --> 00:34:21,433
You've heard already?

626
00:34:21,434 --> 00:34:23,435
So will the traffic congestion

627
00:34:23,436 --> 00:34:26,105
clear up sooner than planned?

628
00:34:28,524 --> 00:34:29,983
Traffic congestion?

629
00:34:29,984 --> 00:34:31,568
Sooner than planned?

630
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:33,029
Sir, we should go.

631
00:34:34,363 --> 00:34:35,698
I'm counting on you.

632
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:38,409
- See you.
- Goodbye.

633
00:34:43,998 --> 00:34:45,458
That's why they're suing?

634
00:34:47,293 --> 00:34:48,419
Ms. Minamida?

635
00:34:55,676 --> 00:34:59,013
BREACH OF CONTRACT
FIRST ORAL ARGUMENT

636
00:34:59,680 --> 00:35:02,809
Plaintiff's counsel,
you may examine the witness.

637
00:35:06,729 --> 00:35:08,271
Ms. Minamida?

638
00:35:08,272 --> 00:35:09,899
Plaintiff's counsel?

639
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:14,486
Yes.

640
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:15,947
Never mind. I'll do it.

641
00:35:16,531 --> 00:35:18,783
I'm Himi, counsel for the plaintiff.

642
00:35:20,409 --> 00:35:21,827
The defendant asked you

643
00:35:21,828 --> 00:35:24,871
to transfer
to Fordee Dance Studio, correct?

644
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:26,833
When was that?

645
00:35:27,583 --> 00:35:28,793
May...

646
00:35:29,460 --> 00:35:31,586
11th, I think.

647
00:35:31,587 --> 00:35:35,383
She asked six of us
in the select class to stay behind.

648
00:35:36,050 --> 00:35:37,135
That's when...

649
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:41,263
So she invited you to transfer

650
00:35:41,264 --> 00:35:43,516
while she was still employed
at Ray Arrows?

651
00:35:46,018 --> 00:35:46,853
Yes.

652
00:35:48,563 --> 00:35:51,524
But you've stayed at Ray Arrows.

653
00:35:52,150 --> 00:35:53,151
Why is that?

654
00:35:55,194 --> 00:35:56,528
Actually...

655
00:35:56,529 --> 00:35:58,531
I wanted to compete too...

656
00:36:01,826 --> 00:36:03,286
But Ms. Saty said

657
00:36:03,953 --> 00:36:08,123
it would be hard for me to do that
and attend cram school.

658
00:36:08,124 --> 00:36:09,292
I see.

659
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:13,753
Poaching talented students
and winning competitions

660
00:36:13,754 --> 00:36:15,381
would be great publicity.

661
00:36:15,965 --> 00:36:18,676
- The defendant's intent...
- What's wrong with that?

662
00:36:24,182 --> 00:36:25,474
I just...

663
00:36:27,143 --> 00:36:29,853
I didn't want their talent to go to waste!

664
00:36:29,854 --> 00:36:33,149
I can help those children
develop their talents!

665
00:36:40,364 --> 00:36:41,698
Making excuses?

666
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:43,491
Poaching is a breach of contract.

667
00:36:43,492 --> 00:36:46,120
Your Honor, she shows no remorse.

668
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:49,749
The defendant will
refrain from interrupting.

669
00:36:50,666 --> 00:36:51,876
I'm sorry.

670
00:36:57,882 --> 00:37:02,260
Regardless of motive, the poaching
appears to breach the contract.

671
00:37:02,261 --> 00:37:04,180
That's my view at present.

672
00:37:07,558 --> 00:37:09,352
Thank you for everything.

673
00:37:14,398 --> 00:37:15,316
Yuma.

674
00:37:16,025 --> 00:37:17,151
Don't stop dancing.

675
00:37:51,310 --> 00:37:52,270
Hello.

676
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:53,896
Hello.

677
00:37:55,481 --> 00:37:58,733
Fordee Dance Studio withdrew
from the competition, I hear.

678
00:37:58,734 --> 00:38:00,528
They just posted a notice.

679
00:38:01,612 --> 00:38:04,323
It seems they wanted
to protect the kids from backlash.

680
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:08,744
Paying damages
will hurt their business too.

681
00:38:11,247 --> 00:38:12,414
Right.

682
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:15,042
This tart's
from the Medical Association head.

683
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:16,710
The Medical Association head?

684
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:19,879
Yes. I'm not sure, but Mr. Himi said

685
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:22,091
it might be thanks
for the Ray Arrows suit.

686
00:38:32,476 --> 00:38:34,186
Excuse me a moment.

687
00:38:38,983 --> 00:38:40,985
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

688
00:38:58,419 --> 00:39:00,671
FORDEE DANCE STUDIO

689
00:39:12,141 --> 00:39:13,684
Hello.

690
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:17,521
Mr. Himi.

691
00:39:18,522 --> 00:39:21,524
How is Ray Arrows linked
to the Medical Association head?

692
00:39:21,525 --> 00:39:23,610
What?

693
00:39:23,611 --> 00:39:26,529
Apparently, his eldest child
went to school

694
00:39:26,530 --> 00:39:28,323
with a Ray Arrows board member.

695
00:39:28,324 --> 00:39:29,575
Is that all?

696
00:39:30,201 --> 00:39:33,162
Watagami Hospital,
being demolished near Fordee...

697
00:39:33,996 --> 00:39:36,331
Isn't it connected to this lawsuit?

698
00:39:36,332 --> 00:39:37,332
I don't know.

699
00:39:37,333 --> 00:39:38,834
Please don't play dumb.

700
00:39:43,672 --> 00:39:45,131
Well...

701
00:39:45,132 --> 00:39:47,259
This is just speculation,

702
00:39:48,469 --> 00:39:50,637
but land that size in that location

703
00:39:50,638 --> 00:39:52,764
could sell for billions of yen.

704
00:39:52,765 --> 00:39:54,558
Maybe tens of billions.

705
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:59,354
However, its property value
also depends on the surrounding area.

706
00:39:59,355 --> 00:40:02,816
If it puts an end to the neighborhood's
chronic traffic congestion,

707
00:40:02,817 --> 00:40:05,027
it'd be worth
the legal costs to the president.

708
00:40:05,611 --> 00:40:08,405
So Ray Arrows was a front

709
00:40:08,406 --> 00:40:09,656
for a SLAPP suit.

710
00:40:09,657 --> 00:40:12,243
That's one way to look at it.

711
00:40:14,036 --> 00:40:16,496
Besides, I think Ms. Minamida

712
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:18,623
had figured that much out too.

713
00:40:18,624 --> 00:40:19,792
What?

714
00:40:20,459 --> 00:40:22,877
That's why she acted strangely

715
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:24,088
at the witness examination.

716
00:40:25,881 --> 00:40:30,761
She and I both worked to maximize
our client's interests.

717
00:40:31,470 --> 00:40:32,721
Isn't that enough?

718
00:40:51,615 --> 00:40:52,658
Ms. Minamida.

719
00:40:55,202 --> 00:40:56,579
What's wrong?

720
00:41:01,584 --> 00:41:02,667
I see.

721
00:41:02,668 --> 00:41:04,837
It's about Fordee Dance Studio.

722
00:41:05,546 --> 00:41:06,505
Yes.

723
00:41:08,841 --> 00:41:09,884
I...

724
00:41:11,135 --> 00:41:13,720
I think I did something unnecessary.

725
00:41:13,721 --> 00:41:15,014
Unnecessary?

726
00:41:16,682 --> 00:41:18,309
The breach of contract suit.

727
00:41:19,852 --> 00:41:23,647
If we'd let the defamation case drag on,

728
00:41:24,565 --> 00:41:27,860
the children might have been
able to compete.

729
00:41:30,488 --> 00:41:32,573
But Ms. Saty said

730
00:41:33,616 --> 00:41:36,660
breach her contract. That's a fact.

731
00:41:37,203 --> 00:41:41,332
So, as a lawyer, you did
the right thing, didn't you?

732
00:41:44,210 --> 00:41:46,754
Even if it was right as a lawyer,

733
00:41:47,671 --> 00:41:51,342
it didn't feel right as Minami Minamida.

734
00:41:51,842 --> 00:41:54,386
But Minami Minamida is a lawyer.

735
00:41:57,681 --> 00:41:59,433
The more I think about it,

736
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:01,894
the less I understand.

737
00:42:06,232 --> 00:42:10,818
Did you know the real purpose
of that lawsuit, Mr. Miyaji?

738
00:42:10,819 --> 00:42:12,947
No. I didn't.

739
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:21,330
Well, I can't quite say that.

740
00:42:23,040 --> 00:42:24,290
If I knew,

741
00:42:24,291 --> 00:42:27,503
I'd have to take a stand
one way or another.

742
00:42:28,045 --> 00:42:29,463
So I avoided knowing.

743
00:42:31,215 --> 00:42:32,383
That's pretty unfair of me.

744
00:42:33,217 --> 00:42:34,635
Yes. It is unfair.

745
00:42:38,472 --> 00:42:40,723
At some point, I started

746
00:42:40,724 --> 00:42:44,853
accepting that this is just
what being a lawyer means.

747
00:42:47,147 --> 00:42:50,108
Will I become like that someday?

748
00:42:50,109 --> 00:42:51,527
That

749
00:42:52,152 --> 00:42:56,699
depends on what kind of lawyer
you want to be, doesn't it?

750
00:42:59,326 --> 00:43:01,287
What kind of lawyer I want to be?

751
00:43:04,582 --> 00:43:05,749
I should get going.

752
00:43:16,010 --> 00:43:18,636
<i>What kind of lawyer...</i>

753
00:43:18,637 --> 00:43:20,264
<i>Do I want to be?</i>

754
00:43:22,224 --> 00:43:25,310
I'd hoped you would
take my case, Ms. Yamaoka.

755
00:43:25,311 --> 00:43:26,769
I'm sorry.

756
00:43:26,770 --> 00:43:29,063
I'd like to take it,

757
00:43:29,064 --> 00:43:32,650
but I'm winding up
my current cases one by one.

758
00:43:32,651 --> 00:43:37,196
Are you following your father
into politics, then?

759
00:43:37,197 --> 00:43:38,657
That's the rumor.

760
00:43:41,785 --> 00:43:44,079
You have my full support.

761
00:43:48,709 --> 00:43:50,001
Come in.

762
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:51,837
Your car is ready.

763
00:43:52,755 --> 00:43:54,005
I'll be going, then.

764
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:55,633
Thank you very much.

765
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:01,763
The documents you requested.

766
00:44:01,764 --> 00:44:02,765
Thank you.

767
00:44:10,397 --> 00:44:11,898
ATTEMPTED MURDER CASE
JUDGMENT

768
00:44:11,899 --> 00:44:13,651
DEFENSE COUNSEL - MIYAJI, MINAMIDA

769
00:44:16,570 --> 00:44:18,572
DEFENSE COUNSEL - MIYAJI, HIMI, MINAMIDA

770
00:44:21,909 --> 00:44:23,827
RAY ARROWS DANCE ACADEMY
YASUO MITSUYA

771
00:44:27,915 --> 00:44:30,917
MINAMI MINAMIDA LAWYER
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LPC

772
00:44:30,918 --> 00:44:31,960
MINAMI MINAMIDA

773
00:44:35,047 --> 00:44:37,132
AN AUTISTIC LAWYER IS BORN!

774
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:49,603
Subtitle translation by:
Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

775
00:44:50,187 --> 00:44:51,896
Those two would make a good couple.

776
00:44:51,897 --> 00:44:55,483
Like my heart's being squeezed
into a salted rice ball.

777
00:44:55,484 --> 00:44:56,692
That's jealousy.

778
00:44:56,693 --> 00:44:58,903
Opposing counsel is Yasuko Yamaoka.

779
00:44:58,904 --> 00:45:01,447
Did you hire Minami
because you could use her?

780
00:45:01,448 --> 00:45:03,908
Let's thoroughly research
this railway project.

781
00:45:03,909 --> 00:45:06,912
<i>Not sure you like him? Try touching him.</i>

782
00:45:07,663 --> 00:45:10,791
<i>Dad, you're always interfering in my life.</i>

783
00:45:11,417 --> 00:45:13,627
I can't even fail on my own!
